  "description": "Built for racing and adventure, the RUUT should be chosen by anyone who wants to ride fast on race day and keep going when the road turns into a forest track. What makes the RUUT exceptionally versatile is the unique TwinTip fork – a feature that allows you to fine tune the handling and set up your bike exactly the way you like – relaxed or racy, the choice is yours to make at any point in time.\n\nThe RUUT CF also features a groundbreaking frame with a unique blend of lowered seat stays, a curved top tube and a revolutionary, interrupted seat tube. This design enhances comfort, safety and speed, moving beyond the classic frame triangle. With a slacker head tube angle, extended reach and higher stack, the bike offers more stability and a more comfortable riding position than the earlier generations of the RUUT. The rear derailleur bolts to a UDH hanger and the threaded T47 bottom bracket is ready for a power meter.\n\nThe RUUT CF 1 is the build with the fewest cables in the family. Shifting is handled by the new wireless Shimano GRX Di2 1x12 groupset – the levers talk to the derailleur over the air, and the low-profile, stabilized derailleur keeps the chain where it belongs when the forest track turns into a rock garden. A wide-range cassette gives you a gear for every wall you meet. The bike rolls on Reynolds G30 wheels with a wide alloy rim covered by a lifetime guarantee and fast rolling WTB Vulpine tires, almost slick in the center and grippy on the shoulders. A Selle Italia Novus Boost saddle sits on top of a carbon seat post that takes the edge out of roots and ruts, and a magnetic Fidlock mount lets you grab your bottle without looking down.",
